c9afb43d6d81" :question/math-academy-id "q-130135" :question/problem "Consider the equation ${y}^{″}+8{y}^{′}+16y=0.$ If $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ is a solution to the equation, then $\\lambda =$" :question/worked-solution "Assuming $y={e}^{\\lambda x}$ and differentiating $y$ with respect to $x$ gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x},\\,{y}^{″}={\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}{e}^{\\lambda x}+8\\lambda {e}^{\\lambda x}+16{e}^{\\lambda x} & =0 \\\\ {e}^{\\lambda x}({\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe auxiliary equation is therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\lambda }^{2}+8\\lambda +16 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactoring the auxiliary equation results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +4)^{2} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand so $\\lambda =-4$ is a repeated root of the auxiliary equation." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-130135/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5fb4d6b-2c86-5ad6-898b-5a1cd44e4106"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130135"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130130/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "754647ea-823c-5165-85ad-fc4b8f2cc120" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130130/selection/d7e416b97cdc7a2a76958b146584f3e9d2dba37c081876d5ccb9edeb765e78c9" :answer/id #uuid "9231044a-d149-5888-bb6c-99ef2fd2c645" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$-14$ or $7$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130130/selection/25666b67a56594dd5245ec05e89d883db07d04362ab51dbc90c39ad20f7f9142" :answer/id #uuid "bd3dde52-172c-55fb-9943-f4d22c58b5fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130130/selection/78d55c628a031620d9c6d475e80034432c10304d0d93320e1ca25a0